WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.140
Drip oil onto water.

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.190
It gathers into droplets
and refuses to mix,

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.910
however long you wait.

4
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.350
Lipids barely dissolve in water.

5
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.040
They are hydrophobic.

6
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:14.350
Yet every cell, from a
bacterium to your own,

7
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.280
is wrapped in a thin film made of lipids.

8
00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:21.460
So how does a film of water-avoiding
molecules build itself?

9
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.830
In this mission, you'll take
one of its molecules apart:

10
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.110
a phospholipid, with a head and two tails.

11
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.890
Then you'll watch the
film assemble in water,

12
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.600
frame by frame.

13
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:37.690
Your mission: find out how a film of
oily molecules builds itself around every

14
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:38.350
cell.
